---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import { BUSINESS, BOOKING_URL, WHATSAPP_URL } from '@/config/site';
import { href } from '@/lib/url';
import {
  graph,
  organizationSchema,
  webSiteSchema,
  webPageSchema,
  breadcrumbSchema,
} from '@/lib/schema';

const title = 'Privacy, what this site does and does not collect | CareInflow';
const description =
  'Plain language: what Microsoft Clarity records when you visit, the two cookies it sets, what we keep when you contact us, and how to have it deleted.';

const schema = graph(
  organizationSchema(),
  webSiteSchema(),
  webPageSchema({ path: '/privacy', title, description }),
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' },
  ]),
);
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} path="/privacy" {schema}>
  <PageHero
    compact
    label="Privacy"
    title="We record how the site is used, not who you are."
    lede="Written in plain language rather than legal boilerplate, because a note nobody can read is not a disclosure. It is short because there is genuinely very little to disclose."
  />

  <div class="border-t border-hairline bg-surface">
    <div class="section shell">
      <div class="prose-ci">
        <h2>What does this website collect?</h2>
        <p>
          Two things, and one of them is new. The pages are static files served
          from a hosting provider which, like every web host, keeps standard
          technical logs such as IP addresses for security and operations. That
          part has not changed, and it is not ours to read.
        </p>
        <p>
          The new part is Microsoft Clarity, added in August 2026. It records
          how this site gets used — where a page was clicked, how far it was
          scrolled, where someone stopped reading — and shows it back to us as
          heatmaps and anonymous session recordings. We added it because page
          design is what we sell, and guessing at which parts of our own pages
          work is a poor way to do that. Microsoft receives what it records as
          well as us, and holds it under their privacy statement.
        </p>
        <p>
          What it does not collect is you. There are no forms anywhere on this
          site — WhatsApp and the phone are the only two ways to reach us — so
          there is nothing typed here for it to capture. It records no name, no
          email address and no phone number, and gives us no way to tell whose
          session we are watching. It sets two cookies on this domain, named
          _clck and _clsk, whose only job is to tell one visit apart from the
          next.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you would rather not be recorded, most content blockers and any
          browser with tracking protection switched on will stop it loading at
          all. Every page here works the same way without it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Two other things on this site are not ours, and both are described
          below: the Google Map in the footer, and the booking link.
        </p>
        <h2>What happens when you contact us?</h2>
        <p>
          WhatsApp and the phone both run through one number. When you message
          or call, we receive your number and what you send. We use it to reply
          and, if you engage us, to do the work. We do not sell it, share it,
          or add you to a mailing list. There is no mailing list.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is one third-party embed on this site, and it is worth naming.
          The footer of every page carries a Google Map showing where the
          studio is. It is set to load lazily and it sits several screens below
          the fold, so nothing is requested from Google until you scroll near
          it — but when you do, Google receives that request and may set its
          own cookies, in the way it does on any page carrying a map. It is not
          analytics: we get no report from it and learn nothing about you
          through it. If you would rather it never loaded, a browser that
          blocks third-party frames will stop it, and the address, the hours
          and the directions link beside it all still work.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is a third contact route, and it is worth being clear about
          because it is the other place a third party is involved. The
          {' '}<a href={BOOKING_URL} rel="noopener">booking link</a> in our
          footer opens Calendly, a scheduling service we do not run. Whatever
          you give it — usually a name, an email address and a time — is held
          by Calendly under their privacy policy as well as reaching us. It is
          a link, not an embed: nothing from Calendly loads on this site unless
          you choose to go there, and nothing of theirs runs on the page you are
          reading. If you would rather not use it, WhatsApp reaches the
          same person.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you would like your contact history deleted, message us and we
          will delete it and confirm.
        </p>
        <h2>Client work and patient privacy</h2>
        <p>
          When we manage a practice's online presence, we sometimes see
          patient-authored content such as public reviews. We treat it with
          the care healthcare deserves: review replies we draft never confirm
          or reveal details of anyone's treatment, and we never request
          access to patient records. We do not need them for anything we do.
        </p>
        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
          Ask us directly on {BUSINESS.phoneDisplay}, by
          {' '}<a href={WHATSAPP_URL} rel="noopener" class="link-whatsapp">WhatsApp</a> or
          {' '}<a href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phone}`} class="prose-link">phone</a>. This note
          was last updated in August 2026 and changes only when our practices do.
          If anything here is unclear, our
          {' '}<a href={href('/contact')} class="prose-link">contact page</a> says what
          happens after you get in touch.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
